<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Codex Bodley</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Codex Bodley is a pre-Hispanic Mixtec <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuscript">manuscript</a> painted on a folded strip of deerskin, now in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bodleian-library">Bodleian Library</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oxford">Oxford</a>. Read in horizontal bands, it records the genealogies, marriages and wars of the ruling families of Tilantongo and other Mixtec kingdoms of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oaxaca">Oaxaca</a> from the 10th century to the early 16th, including the career of the ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eight-deer-jaguar-claw">Eight Deer Jaguar Claw</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/codex-bodley.jpg" alt="Codex Bodley" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jononmac46 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Codex_Bodley_(1).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
